---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import LegalAddress from '../components/LegalAddress.astro';
import LegalEntity from '../components/LegalEntity.astro';
import { brandName } from '../lib/site';
import content from '../lib/content';

const { entity, consultant, contactEmail, termsUpdated } = content.legal;
---

<Legal
  title={`Terms of service - ${brandName}`}
  description={`The terms governing your use of ${brandName}: an experimental, AI-assisted consulting platform operated by ${entity}.`}
  path="/terms"
  heading="Terms of service"
  updated={termsUpdated}
>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of <strong>{brandName}</strong> (the "Platform"), a service
    operated by <strong><LegalEntity /></strong>, represented by {consultant} ("we", "us").<LegalAddress
    /> By creating an account or using the Platform you accept these terms. If you use the Platform on
    behalf of a company, you confirm you are authorized to bind it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>The Platform offers two delivery modes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Curated AI MVP</strong> ("AI-curated works"): AI agents build a software MVP under the direction and supervision of {consultant}. You follow the build live, read the code as pull requests, and approve the delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct quote</strong>: a bespoke engagement hand-built by {consultant}, scoped and priced through a custom quote.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The Platform is in <strong>alpha</strong>. It is an <strong>experimental product</strong>,
    provided without any availability commitment or service-level agreement. Features may change,
    be interrupted, or be withdrawn at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Experimental product - AI-curated works and liability</h2>
  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>AI-curated works are experimental and delivered "as is".</strong> Any work produced
      by AI agents through the Platform does not engage <LegalEntity /> in any liability, to the
      maximum extent permitted by applicable law. This is an experimental product: you are solely
      responsible for reviewing, testing, and validating every AI-curated deliverable before any
      use, and for any consequence of using it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    <LegalEntity /> gives no warranty, express or implied, that AI-curated works are free of defects,
    secure, fit for a particular purpose, or compliant with regulations applicable to your
    activity. Human review by {consultant} is a quality practice, not a guarantee of the
    output. Where applicable law does not allow a full exclusion of liability (in particular in
    case of gross negligence, willful misconduct, or mandatory consumer rights), <LegalEntity />'s
    total liability is capped at the amounts you paid for the project concerned in the 12 months
    preceding the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>3. MVP only - do not use against production infrastructure</h2>
  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>AI-curated works are for MVP and demonstration purposes only.</strong> We strongly
      advise against running, connecting, or deploying an AI-curated work on or against
      production infrastructure, production data, or any system whose failure could cause harm.
      This is for MVP!
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>For production deployments, use the Direct quote path:</strong> a production-grade
      engagement reviewed, hardened, and delivered by {consultant} under a separate,
      explicitly agreed scope.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    If you nonetheless choose to use an AI-curated work in production or against production
    systems, you do so entirely at your own risk and against our express advice, and you release
    <LegalEntity /> from any resulting claim to the maximum extent permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must provide accurate information and keep your credentials confidential; you are responsible for activity under your account.</li>
    <li>A verified email address is required before creating a project, because project lifecycle notifications are sent by email.</li>
    <li>We may suspend or close accounts that breach these terms or threaten the security of the Platform.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Credits, quotes, and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Curated AI MVPs are paid with <strong>prepaid credits</strong> (1 credit = 1 EUR), topped up through Stripe. Builds consume credits based on actual AI usage, metered live on your dashboard.</li>
    <li>Estimates shown before a build are good-faith estimates, not fixed prices; actual consumption may differ.</li>
    <li>Direct-quote work is priced by a custom quote you explicitly accept before work starts. Submitting a request is free.</li>
    <li>Credits are not transferable between organizations. For questions about refunds of unused credits, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>; statutory rights, where applicable, are unaffected.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Your content and obligations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You warrant that the content you submit (project descriptions, attachments, code, credentials) is lawful and that you hold the rights needed to share it.</li>
    <li>You must not request work that is illegal, infringes third-party rights, or falls under our review triggers for prohibited or sensitive actions (for example malicious tooling or acting on infrastructure you do not control); such requests are refused or routed to human review.</li>
    <li>Credentials you store in project Memory are shared at your own initiative so the build agent can use them; scope them to the minimum access needed and rotate them after the engagement.</li>
    <li>You must not attempt to probe, disrupt, or access data on the Platform that is not yours.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Upon full payment, the code delivered to your repository for your project is yours.</li>
    <li><LegalEntity /> retains all rights to the Platform itself, its knowledge base, prompts, tooling, and pre-existing know-how, which are licensed to no one through a delivery.</li>
    <li>Deliverables may include open-source components, which remain governed by their own licenses.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Demos</h2>
  <p>
    Live demos run on temporary, password-protected subdomains for evaluation only. They are not
    hosting: demos can be stopped, restarted, or removed at any time and carry no uptime or data
    persistence commitment.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You can close your account at any time. We can terminate or suspend access for breach of
    these terms, with notice where reasonably possible. Sections 2, 3, and 7 survive termination.
    Personal data is handled as described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the service evolves. Material changes are announced on the
    Platform or by email before they take effect; continued use after that constitutes
    acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of the country where <LegalEntity /> is established. Any dispute
    that cannot be resolved amicably is submitted to the competent courts of that country, without
    prejudice to mandatory jurisdiction rules protecting consumers.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
